Mon Oct 26 08:20:36 UTC 2026 - Dirk Müller <dmueller@suse.com>

- update to 2.3.0:
  * Added optional support for USB FIDO2 security keys, installed
    with the fido2 extra.
  * Added Launchpad.register_hardware_key() to register security
    keys on the logged-in account.
  * Added Launchpad.issue_hardware_bound_oauth_token() and
    Launchpad.revoke_hardware_bound_oauth_token() to manage OAuth
    refresh grants bound to a security key.
  * Added Launchpad.login_with_hardware_token(), which exchanges
    a hardware-bound grant for short-lived access tokens and
    stores only the grant.
  * Hardened security posture.
  * Updated link to homepage.
  * Added pysocks dependency for proxy support in httplib2.
  * Added support for Python 3.14.
  * Replaced deprecated pkg_resources usage with
    importlib.resources.
  * Fixed login_with() so that consumer_name performs a single-
    application integration instead of being discarded in favour
    of a desktop-wide one, and forwarded allow_access_levels so
    applications can request narrower permissions than
    DESKTOP_INTEGRATION.

